pagewire: make fork() wait until no other thread holds a pthread lock.

libcupsfilters 2.1.1 (cfFilterChain(), cfFilterPOpen()) and libppd 2.1.1
fork without exec and run filter functions in the child, while PAPPL serves
IPP clients on other threads. A lock another thread holds at that moment
(libcups' string pool mutex, a PAPPL rwlock, glibc's tzset lock) stays
locked in the child, and the job hangs in "processing" for good.

This patch is pagewire's own: it adds pappl-retrofit/fork-gate.c to the
library. Upstream report, open and unfixed:
https://github.com/OpenPrinting/pappl-retrofit/issues/35
Drop this patch, images/driver/fork-gate-test.c and the fork gate steps in
images/driver/Dockerfile once that issue is fixed: when libcupsfilters and
libppd no longer run filter functions in a forked child, or pappl-retrofit
no longer calls them from a multi-threaded process.

